  "_comment": [
    "Frozen query set for the retrieval regression gate. See",
    "docs/TOPIC_LAYER_PLAN.md 8.5 and 18.1 item A6.",
    "",
    "This replaces the labelled baseline v6.2 asked for, which cannot be",
    "built: evaluate_phase2.py consumes exported human relevance labels, the",
    "label corpus is deliberately private, and producing one means a labelling",
    "campaign outside this project's scope. This set needs no judgments. It",
    "compares a build against its own prior self, so it answers 'did retrieval",
    "change?' -- which is the question 0.5 actually asks -- and says nothing",
    "about whether a change was an improvement. Judging improvement still needs",
    "labels, and that is still unsolved (issues #8 and #9).",
    "",
    "The catalog is the 8.4 hermetic build's output, so both gates run over one",
    "fixture set. Stated plainly: it holds 5 records, so 'top 50' and 'top 10'",
    "are in practice 'everything that matched'. The value here is breadth of",
    "CODE PATH -- tokenizer, stemmer, acronym resolver, exact-number match,",
    "coverage gating, profile term building, applicant-fit bonus -- not",
    "statistical power over a large corpus. A query that returns nothing is",
    "carrying real signal: it proves the admission rules still reject.",
    "",
    "kinds: keyword | acronym | number | empty_expected | profile"
  ],
